00:03:32.910 --> 00:03:36.960
[inaudible] does that fall under what you're
describing or is that maybe outside of it?

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:38.420
It's actually outside of it.

00:03:38.420 --> 00:03:44.720
This is a question I get a lot, uh, is, is
there something, um, addictive about capitalism

00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:47.120
or consumerism itself?

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:51.970
And I don't really go there because I think
that that's, that's just pushing it too hard.

00:03:51.970 --> 00:03:57.320
If someone's in the hardware business and
they're competing to sell you the latest lawn

00:03:57.320 --> 00:04:04.680
mower or you know, new gutters for your house
or whatever, they may resort to advertising.

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:06.780
You may be keeping up with the Joneses.

00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:09.300
But that's not the same thing as an addiction.

00:04:09.300 --> 00:04:13.450
An addiction is something that involves, um,
loss of control.

00:04:13.450 --> 00:04:19.760
It involves craving preoccupation, and it
involves fairly serious harms to both yourself,

00:04:19.760 --> 00:04:21.860
your family and to society.

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:31.520
And so I, I, to me that's not garden variety
